<div id="static-navigation-tabs">
  <h1>Navigation Tabs CSS Component</h1>

  <p>
    A navigation tab <em>looks</em> like a normal tab, but is actually a
    hyperlink to a new page. Therefore a set of navigation tabs behaves more
    like a simple navigational widget, rather than a dynamic user interface
    control.
  </p>
  <p>
    If HREF is not present, then the tab will be in disabled state. A value of
    "javascript" (or any such variant) is <strong>not</strong> a valid URL!
  </p>
  <p>
    The <code>aria-current</code> attribute is used to programmatically denote
    the current page state and current link.
  </p>

  <p>
    Use child element modifier <code>navigation-tabs--large</code> to opt into
    larger font-size for navigation tabs.
  </p>

